# Invariants every preset entry must honor -- both are contrast requirements
# that the token system cannot enforce for you:
#
# 1. "dark_tokens" must always set "--site-accent". It is never optional. The
#    base "tokens" accent is chosen to pass contrast on a light page; if
#    "dark_tokens" omits it, that light-mode accent leaks into dark mode and
#    will generally fail contrast against the dark background. The same
#    applies to "--site-accent-hover": every preset below sets it in both
#    "tokens" and "dark_tokens" for the same reason.
#
# 2. "--site-accent-solid" must never be set to a preset's dark-mode
#    "--site-accent" value. It fills a button solid behind white text, so it
#    sits on neither side of the light/dark boundary and is deliberately not
#    overridden in dark mode -- it has to stay dark enough for white text at
#    all times. Every preset below sets it to the same light-mode-safe value
#    as its base "--site-accent"; follow that pattern.
